<figure class="lifecycle" data-lifecycle aria-labelledby="r12-lifecycle-title"><figcaption id="r12-lifecycle-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Leaving the parent is not leaving storage</figcaption>
 <div class="parent"><p class="panel-label">Parent: request_events</p><div class="pieces"><div class="piece" data-attached>September · E1</div><div class="piece">October · E2, E3</div><div class="piece">November · E4</div></div><p data-parent-count data-live>Queries of the parent can see 4 rows.</p></div>
 <div class="separate"><p class="panel-label">Standalone table after detach</p><div class="piece" data-detached hidden>events_sep · E1</div><p data-separate-count data-live>No detached table yet.</p></div>
 <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p><div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 2 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <p class="caption">An illustrative retirement sequence. September begins attached; after a checked detach, the parent has three rows and the separate table still has E1. Dropping that table is a later policy decision. The worksheet verifies detach and reattach, including a reference that prevents detach; it does not measure an archival service or erase backups.</p>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-lifecycle]').forEach(root=>{const text=['September is still part of the parent. Check the entire month’s eligibility, its references and the policy for late September writes before removing it.','The removal gate has passed in this illustration: eligible contents, references resolved and old writes rejected or separately routed. No table has moved yet.','DETACH removes September from the parent’s partition map. E1 remains stored in events_sep and can be queried directly.','Only a separate DROP removes the detached table. Retained exports, archives and backups still have their own policies.'];stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw:(s:number)=>{root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-attached]')!.hidden=s>=2;root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-detached]')!.hidden=s!==2;root.querySelector('[data-parent-count]')!.textContent=`Queries of the parent can see ${s>=2?3:4} rows.`;root.querySelector('[data-separate-count]')!.textContent=s<2?'No detached table yet.':s===2?'E1 is retained here. It has not been deleted.':'The standalone table has been dropped in this illustration.';root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=text[s];}});});
</script>
<style>.lifecycle{padding:1rem;margin:2rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);font:.9rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.2rem var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:1rem}figcaption span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.7rem}.parent{border:2px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.9rem}.separate{border:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.9rem;margin:1rem 0}.panel-label{font-weight:600;margin-top:0}.pieces{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.7rem}.piece{padding:.7rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);background:var(--color-surface)}[hidden]{display:none}.controls{display:flex;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}button{font:inherit;padding:.45rem .65rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);border-radius:.25rem;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);cursor:pointer}button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.5}button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}[data-explanation]{min-height:4.5em;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.8rem}[data-hold]{height:3px;width:100%;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{display:block;width:0;height:100%;background:var(--color-accent)}.caption{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}</style>
